/* PATHDATA: research for "My Path". Every fact was read from an official or university page on the date in last_checked, with its source link.
   Anything not confirmed is listed under "unverified" and shown to the student as "check the official site". Do not add numbers without a source. */
const PATH_DEST = {"usa":{"id":"usa","name":"United States","last_checked":"2026-10-13","overview":"Students apply directly to each college. EducationUSA describes five steps: research options, finance studies, complete application, apply for student visa, prepare for departure, and advises starting the search at least 12 to 18 months before the intended start. Requirements, deadlines and test policies are set by each college.","admission_model":"Many colleges accept the Common App, a shared application; each college sets its own requirements and deadlines, and fee waivers exist via the Common App or college-specific waivers. Per EducationUSA, there is no official ranking system and each institution sets its own graduation requirements. Colleges may offer early and regular deadlines (University of Michigan: Early Decision and Early Action Nov. 1, Regular Decision Feb. 1 for the 2026-2027 cycle). The word 'holistic' appears on Princeton's page ('Standardized testing is but one element of our comprehensive and holistic application review process'); no neutral government description of holistic review was opened.","tests":[{"name":"SAT/ACT","policy":"Varies by university: Common App says some colleges always require scores, others are flexible or test optional. Check each target college's own page for the exact cycle.","examples":[{"university":"MIT","statement":"'We require the SAT or the ACT.' ACT writing/science and SAT essay not required. Tests must be taken before Nov 30 (Early Action) or Dec 31 (Regular Action). The page does not name the cycle.","source":"https://mitadmissions.org/apply/firstyear/tests-scores/"},{"university":"University of Michigan","statement":"2026-2027 cycle: 'SAT or ACT score, if available.' To have a score considered, self-report by Nov. 1 for Early Action; applicants may indicate they do not want a score considered.","source":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/requirements-deadlines"},{"university":"Princeton University","statement":"Page states testing is one element of holistic review; the specific test requirement was not shown on the page opened (linked separate page failed to load).","source":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/international-students"},{"university":"University of Arizona","statement":"Page opened covers English tests; an SAT/ACT policy statement was not found there.","source":"https://www.arizona.edu/admissions/undergraduate/international"}],"source":"https://commonapp.org/apply/first-year-students"}],"english":[{"test":"MIT (TOEFL, IELTS, Duolingo, PTE)","note":"Strongly recommended if English used fewer than five years or not spoken at home/school. IELTS min 7 (rec. 7.5); TOEFL taken before 1/21/26 min 90 (rec. 100); TOEFL on/after 1/21/26 min 5 (rec. 5.5) on 1-6 scale; Duolingo min 120 (rec. 125); PTE min 65 (rec. 70).","source":"https://mitadmissions.org/apply/firstyear/tests-scores/"},{"test":"University of Michigan (TOEFL, IELTS, others)","note":"Required if English is second language. TOEFL iBT '100 range' with section scores 23+ listening/reading and 21+ speaking/writing; TOEFL from Jan 21 2026 '5-6 range' with sections 5+; IELTS '7.0 range' with sections 6.5+. Duolingo is not mentioned on the page. Egypt is not on the exemption country list.","source":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/exams-visas"},{"test":"University of Arizona","note":"Undergraduate minimums: IELTS 6.5; Duolingo 110; TOEFL iBT 79 (before Jan 2026) or 4 (after Jan 2026) as listed. Scores must be dated within 2 years of application. IGCSE/O Level English grade C or higher can also qualify. All documents must be in English.","source":"https://www.arizona.edu/admissions/undergraduate/international"},{"test":"Princeton University","note":"Applicants from non-English schools take TOEFL, IELTS Academic, Duolingo or PTE Academic; exempt after 3 years at a secondary school where English is the primary language of instruction. No minimum scores seen.","source":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/international-students"}],"documents":[{"name":"Application (Common App or college's own) and fee","note":"University of Michigan: Common App with $75 fee (2026-2027 cycle). Fee waivers available via Common App or college-specific.","source":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/requirements-deadlines"},{"name":"High school transcript","note":"EducationUSA: an original transcript is required for each institution. Michigan: include official English translation if not in English, and final transcript with graduation date if finished.","source":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/requirements-deadlines"},{"name":"Teacher evaluation / school report / counselor recommendation","note":"Michigan 2026-2027: School Report and one Teacher Evaluation; counselor recommendation encouraged. Varies by college.","source":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/requirements-deadlines"},{"name":"Test scores (SAT/ACT) if required or chosen","note":"Varies by college.","source":"https://commonapp.org/apply/first-year-students"},{"name":"English proficiency score","note":"Varies by college; see english section.","source":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/exams-visas"},{"name":"Financial documentation","note":"Michigan states students enrolling must provide proof of full financial support before the I-20 is issued and complete the Financial Resources Statement.","source":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/exams-visas"}],"timeline":[{"when":"12-18 months before the intended start (about the start of Grade 11 for a September start)","step":"EducationUSA advises beginning the college search at least 12 to 18 months before the academic year.","source":"https://educationusa.state.gov/your-5-steps-us-study/research-your-options/undergraduate"},{"when":"Before the application deadlines; sit required tests early","step":"MIT: required tests taken before Nov 30 (Early Action) or Dec 31 (Regular Action). Michigan: self-report score by Nov 1 for Early Action.","source":"https://mitadmissions.org/apply/firstyear/tests-scores/"},{"when":"Autumn of final school year","step":"Michigan 2026-2027 cycle deadlines: Early Decision Nov. 1; Early Action Nov. 1; Regular Decision Feb. 1. Michigan advises applicants far from the US to apply as early as possible. Deadlines vary by university.","source":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/requirements-deadlines"},{"when":"After admission","step":"School enters you in SEVIS and issues Form I-20; pay SEVIS I-901 fee; attend visa interview. Student visa can be issued up to 365 days before the course starts; entry no earlier than 30 days before start.","source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas/study/student-visa.html"}],"visa":{"summary":"Per travel.state.gov: school issues Form I-20 via SEVIS, signed by student and school official and presented at the interview. SEVIS I-901 fee paid after acceptance (amount on ICE SEVIS site, not on this page). Visa can be issued up to 365 days before course start; entry limited to 30 days before. Interviews are generally required. The consular officer may ask how you will pay educational, living and travel costs. University of Michigan: most international students use F-1; I-20 issued after proof of full financial support.","source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas/study/student-visa.html"},"funding":[{"name":"EducationUSA financial aid guidance","note":"States international students receive significant financial assistance each year but competition is high; aid applications go together with admission applications; institutions may offer scholarships, in-state tuition benefits, waived fees. Points to 'Find financial aid' resource.","url":"https://educationusa.state.gov/your-5-steps-us-study/finance-your-studies"},{"name":"Princeton University financial aid","note":"Need-based only, no merit scholarships; admission need-blind; full demonstrated need of admitted international students met; grants rather than loans.","url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/international-students"},{"name":"University of Michigan","note":"Example of the opposite policy: international students on temporary visas are not eligible for financial aid and are expected to pay full cost of attendance.","url":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-students"}],"egyptian_notes":[{"note":"EducationUSA Egypt has a center at the U.S. Embassy in Cairo (contact by email form on the page; Facebook and Instagram listed). Also listed in search: EducationUSA at AMIDEAST Cairo and Alexandria (pages not opened).","source":"https://educationusa.state.gov/centers/educationusa-egypt-us-embassy-cairo"},{"note":"University of Michigan: Egypt is not on its English-exemption country list, so Egyptian applicants should expect to submit an English test. Michigan also has a 'Requirements by Country' page that failed to load.","source":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/exams-visas"}],"universities":[{"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","country":"United States","why_example":"Highly selective private","requirements":"SAT or ACT required. English test strongly recommended in some cases (IELTS min 7; Duolingo min 120). Tests before Nov 30 (EA) / Dec 31 (RA).","url":"https://mitadmissions.org/apply/firstyear/tests-scores/"},{"name":"University of Michigan","country":"United States","why_example":"Large public, flexible test policy","requirements":"2026-2027: Common App, $75 fee, SAT/ACT if available, School Report + teacher evaluation, transcript; English test (TOEFL ~100 range / IELTS ~7.0 range). ED/EA Nov 1, RD Feb 1.","url":"https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/requirements-deadlines"},{"name":"University of Arizona","country":"United States","why_example":"Mid-size/large public","requirements":"English minimums: IELTS 6.5, Duolingo 110, TOEFL 79 (pre Jan 2026). Documents in English. Deadlines and test policy not verified.","url":"https://www.arizona.edu/admissions/undergraduate/international"}],"key_links":[{"label":"EducationUSA: 5 steps","url":"https://educationusa.state.gov/your-5-steps-us-study"},{"label":"EducationUSA Egypt (US Embassy Cairo)","url":"https://educationusa.state.gov/centers/educationusa-egypt-us-embassy-cairo"},{"label":"US Dept of State student visa","url":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas/study/student-visa.html"},{"label":"Common App first-year","url":"https://commonapp.org/apply/first-year-students"}],"unverified":["Princeton testing requirement and deadlines (pages failed)","University of Arizona SAT/ACT policy and deadlines; arizona.edu country-specific Egypt info","MIT Early/Regular application dates and cycle name (page does not state)","Official visa-specific proof-of-funds amounts (State Dept page gives none)","Egyptian Thanaweya Amma / Egyptian Baccalaureate evaluation by US colleges (Michigan requirements-by-country page failed)","eg.usembassy.gov study-in-USA page failed to load","SEVIS I-901 fee amount","Official US government scholarships for international undergraduates (none identified; Fulbright etc. not checked)","Neutral official description of holistic review"],"flag":"🇺🇸"},"uk":{"id":"uk","name":"United Kingdom","last_checked":"2026-10-13","cycle":"2027 entry (applications open since 12 May 2026). The next cycle (2028 entry) was not checked.","overview":"Undergraduate applications to UK universities are made through UCAS. Each university sets its own entry requirements, so Egyptian applicants must check every course. Universities differ sharply on Thanaweya Amma: Oxford lists it as 'Not accepted', Cambridge says it alone is unlikely to be competitive, and Manchester accepts it only for a foundation year first. Note: for 2027 entry the UCAS equal-consideration dates are 15 October 2026 and 13 January 2027 (not 14/15 January).","admission_model":"Apply online via UCAS: up to five choices for a fee of £34.50 for 2027 entry (Oxford and Cambridge: usually only one of the two; medicine/dentistry/veterinary: max four such courses). Application has 13 sections including a 4,000-character personal statement and a reference from someone who is not a family member or friend. Qualifications must be entered with titles as on the certificate. International applicants can enter English test results and, for 2027 entry, upload English certificates and passport evidence through a UCAS document upload service. Universities decide offers; many continue to accept international applications after January.","tests":[{"name":"SAT / ACT","policy":"None of the UCAS pages opened describe SAT or ACT as a general requirement for UK undergraduate entry. Individual universities may mention them only for specific applicant groups (Cambridge mentions SAT/ACT with AP tests for China and the US sections; Oxford's page mentions SAT/AP for Canada). For Egyptian applicants no SAT/ACT requirement was found on pages opened. Check each university.","examples":[{"university":"University of Cambridge","statement":"For Egypt, lists the Thanaweya Amma/Al-Azhar certificate and Egyptian STEM Diploma as needing further study (examples given: A Levels, IB, or 5+ AP tests at score 5 with an overall General Secondary School Certificate score of at least 95%). SAT/ACT is mentioned only in other country sections.","source":"https://www.undergraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/egypt"}],"source":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/you-apply/what-and-where-study/entry-requirements"},{"name":"Admissions tests (examples only): UCAT, LNAT, TMUA, ESAT, TARA","policy":"Some courses require an admissions test; this varies by university and course. Examples for the 2026-27 cycle at Oxford: UCAT (Medicine), LNAT (Law), TMUA (Computer Science, Mathematics), ESAT (e.g. Engineering Science, Physics, Biomedical Sciences), TARA (e.g. Philosophy, Politics and Economics). Some tests are taken before the UCAS deadline.","examples":[{"university":"University of Oxford","statement":"UAT-UK (ESAT/TMUA/TARA) October sitting: test booking closed 28 Sep 2026; tests 12-16 Oct 2026; results 16 Nov 2026. UCAT and LNAT run through Pearson.","source":"https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/undergraduate/applying-to-oxford/guide/admissions-tests"},{"university":"University of Cambridge (2027 entry)","statement":"ESAT/TMUA sitting 12-16 Oct 2026 (registration closed 28 Sep 2026); LNAT by 15 Oct 2026 (registration closed 15 Sep 2026); UCAT by 24 Sep 2026 (registration closed 16 Sep 2026).","source":"https://www.undergraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/apply/application-dates-deadlines"}],"source":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/you-apply/what-and-where-study/entry-requirements"},{"name":"UCAT (medicine and dentistry, used by many universities)","policy":"UCAT 2026 registration and booking is closed (booking deadline 16 Sep 2026; last test day 24 Sep 2026; UCAS deadline 15 Oct 2026). The page does not state an entry year; instructions for UCAT 2027 will be published later. Whether Egypt test centres exist was not verified.","examples":[],"source":"https://www.ucat.ac.uk/about-ucat/ucat-test-dates/"}],"english":[{"test":"General (UCAS)","note":"The level needed varies by university. Students who need a Student visa may need a test approved by UKVI. UCAS lists IELTS, TOEFL, Trinity ISE, PTE, and Cambridge C1 Advanced/C2 Proficiency as accepted tests, with IELTS or TOEFL numbers enterable in the application.","source":"https://www.ucas.com/international/international-students/support-for-international-students/tips-for-international-applications"},{"test":"University of Oxford (example)","note":"IELTS Academic overall 7.5 with at least 7.0 in each component (IELTS Online not accepted); TOEFL iBT 110 with minimums L22/R24/S25/W24; TOEFL taken from 21 Jan 2026 not accepted. Oxford confirms English on the CAS, so no extra English evidence is needed for the visa.","source":"https://ox.ac.uk/admissions/undergraduate/applying-to-oxford/for-international-students/ELR"},{"test":"University of Manchester (example)","note":"All applicants must show English proficiency; UKVI requires at least B2; individual Schools may set higher levels and some need the score before applying. IGCSE/O-level English may be considered in certain circumstances. Exact scores per course were not on the page.","source":"https://www.manchester.ac.uk/study/international/country-specific-information/egypt/entry-requirements/"}],"documents":[{"name":"Qualifications and grades entered in UCAS","note":"All qualifications from secondary education onwards, including results awaited. Some universities want certificates or transcripts only after an offer (Oxford) or earlier (Cambridge asks for a transcript by 22 Oct 2026 for 2027 entry).","source":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/applying-to-university/filling-in-your-ucas-application"},{"name":"Personal statement","note":"One statement of up to 4,000 characters. The page refers to the guide for '2026 entry onwards'; the exact question structure was not stated on the page.","source":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/applying-to-university/writing-your-personal-statement"},{"name":"Reference","note":"Required for every application; from a school, college or UCAS registered centre; not family, friend or partner.","source":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/applying-to-university/filling-in-your-ucas-application"},{"name":"English test certificate and passport/immigration evidence","note":"Can be uploaded through the UCAS document upload service for 2027 entry.","source":"https://ucas.com/international/international-students/applying-university-international-student"},{"name":"UK ENIC Statement of Comparability (optional)","note":"UK ENIC can provide a statement comparing qualifications with UK equivalents; the UCAS entry names UK ENIC. Whether any university requires it was not verified.","source":"https://www.enic.org.uk/"},{"name":"Student visa documents","note":"Valid passport and a CAS from the university are always required; proof of funds, TB test results if needed, financial sponsor consent if applicable, parental consent if under 18.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/student-visa/documents-you-must-provide"}],"timeline":[{"when":"Up to the start of the final school year (spring-summer before)","step":"UCAS began showing 2027 courses on 28 Apr 2026 and applications opened on 12 May 2026. Take UCAT or other required tests (UCAT booking deadline was 16 Sep 2026).","source":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/applying-to-university/dates-and-deadlines-for-uni-applications"},{"when":"Start of final school year (September)","step":"Completed UCAS applications can be submitted from 1 Sep 2026.","source":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/applying-to-university/dates-and-deadlines-for-uni-applications"},{"when":"Early in final school year (October)","step":"15 Oct 2026, 18:00 UK time: deadline for Oxford, Cambridge, and most medicine, dentistry and veterinary courses. Cambridge also requires its own form by 22 Oct 2026 and a transcript by 22 Oct 2026. Oxford written work due to colleges by 10 Nov; interviews early-mid Dec; offers 12 Jan 2027.","source":"https://www.undergraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/apply/application-dates-deadlines"},{"when":"Middle of final school year (January)","step":"13 Jan 2027, 18:00 UK time: equal-consideration date for most undergraduate courses.","source":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/applying-to-university/dates-and-deadlines-for-uni-applications"},{"when":"After January","step":"25 Feb 2027 Extra opens; 30 Jun 2027 is the last date for applications to be sent to universities before Clearing; 2 Jul 2027 Clearing opens; 23 Sep 2027 is the final date for 2027 entry applications. UCAS says many universities accept international applications later in the year, but time is needed for visa and accommodation.","source":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/applying-to-university/dates-and-deadlines-for-uni-applications"},{"when":"After receiving an offer and CAS","step":"Student visa can be applied for up to 6 months before the course starts; decisions usually take about 3 weeks from outside the UK.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/student-visa"}],"visa":{"summary":"Student visa: age 16 or over, an offer from a licensed student sponsor (CAS), enough money, and English ability. Apply up to 6 months before the course starts; decision usually about 3 weeks from outside the UK. Fee shown: £558 from outside the UK; the healthcare surcharge is paid separately. Maintenance funds (per gov.uk): £1,529 per month in London, £1,171 per month outside London, for up to 9 months, held for 28 consecutive days ending within 31 days of the application date. Whether Egyptian applicants need a TB test was not stated on the pages opened. Amounts change; confirm on gov.uk before applying.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/student-visa"},"funding":[{"name":"Undergraduate scholarships for international students","note":"Study UK states undergraduate scholarships are less common than postgraduate but come from UK universities and from third parties such as governments or organisations in the home country. It names no specific undergraduate scheme and does not mention Egypt.","url":"https://study-uk.britishcouncil.org/scholarships-funding"},{"name":"Chevening / GREAT / Commonwealth","note":"Study UK describes Chevening as fully funded master's degrees and GREAT Scholarships as one-year master's courses; they are postgraduate, so not applicable to bachelor applicants.","url":"https://study-uk.britishcouncil.org/scholarships-funding"},{"name":"University-specific scholarships","note":"University of Manchester has an Egypt scholarships page (listed in search results, not opened).","url":"https://www.manchester.ac.uk/study/international/country-specific-information/egypt/scholarships/"}],"egyptian_notes":[{"note":"Oxford international qualifications page lists Egypt's Thanaweya A'ama (General Secondary School Certificate) as 'Not accepted' to meet its standard offer.","source":"https://ox.ac.uk/admissions/undergraduate/applying-to-oxford/for-international-students/international-qualifications?wssl=1"},{"note":"Cambridge Egypt section: Certificate of Nile International Secondary Education (CNISE) offers are based on A level minimum requirements; Thanaweya Amma/Al-Azhar certificate or Egyptian STEM Diploma alone 'will not be competitive and are unlikely to be successful', and further study (A Levels, IB, or 5+ APs at 5 with at least 95% overall) is strongly recommended. The Egyptian Baccalaureate and IGCSEs are not mentioned.","source":"https://www.undergraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/egypt"},{"note":"Manchester Egypt page: Thanaweya Amma holders enter a foundation year first (integrated science/engineering foundation year needs overall 90%+ with 90%+ in Maths and Physics; INTO Manchester foundation programmes need 85%+ overall). The page does not mention the Egyptian Baccalaureate and does not state the entry year it applies to.","source":"https://www.manchester.ac.uk/study/international/country-specific-information/egypt/entry-requirements/"},{"note":"UCAS says universities set their own entry requirements, many accept equivalent international qualifications, and UK ENIC can provide a comparison statement. The UCAS Egypt country page could not be opened, so no UCAS Egypt-specific statement is verified.","source":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/you-apply/what-and-where-study/entry-requirements"},{"note":"UCL offers Undergraduate Preparatory Certificates (foundation courses) for international students who cannot enter a UCL degree directly; the page does not mention Egypt.","source":"https://www.ucl.ac.uk/study/undergraduate-preparatory-certificates-ucls-international-foundation-year"}],"universities":[{"name":"University of Oxford","country":"United Kingdom","why_example":"Highly selective; own tests and earliest deadline.","requirements":"UCAS deadline 15 Oct 2026 (2027 entry); admissions tests by course; Thanaweya A'ama listed as not accepted for the standard offer; IELTS Academic 7.5 overall / 7.0 each component, or TOEFL iBT 110.","url":"https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/undergraduate/applying-to-oxford/for-international-students/international-qualifications"},{"name":"University of Manchester","country":"United Kingdom","why_example":"Large research university with a published Egypt page and foundation route for Thanaweya Amma.","requirements":"Thanaweya Amma: foundation year first (85-90%+ depending on route). English: UKVI minimum B2, higher by School. Entry-year of the page not stated.","url":"https://www.manchester.ac.uk/study/international/country-specific-information/egypt/entry-requirements/"},{"name":"UCL","country":"United Kingdom","why_example":"London university that offers its own foundation certificates for international students.","requirements":"Entry requirements pages do not mention Egypt; country-specific requirements are shown on course pages; English requirements in a separate guide (not opened); Undergraduate Preparatory Certificates exist for students who cannot enter directly.","url":"https://www.ucl.ac.uk/study/prospective-students/undergraduate/how-apply/entry-requirements"}],"key_links":[{"label":"UCAS: dates and deadlines","url":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/applying-to-university/dates-and-deadlines-for-uni-applications"},{"label":"UCAS: international students","url":"https://ucas.com/international/international-students/applying-university-international-student"},{"label":"UCAS: filling in your application","url":"https://www.ucas.com/applying/applying-to-university/filling-in-your-ucas-application"},{"label":"GOV.UK Student visa","url":"https://www.gov.uk/student-visa"},{"label":"GOV.UK Student visa: money needed","url":"https://www.gov.uk/student-visa/money"},{"label":"Study UK (British Council)","url":"https://study-uk.britishcouncil.org/"},{"label":"UK ENIC","url":"https://www.enic.org.uk/"},{"label":"UCAT test dates","url":"https://www.ucat.ac.uk/about-ucat/ucat-test-dates/"}],"unverified":["UCAS Egypt country page (https://www.ucas.com/international/countries/egypt) and the UCAS key-dates page under undergraduate/ could not be opened (fetch error); UCAS Egypt-specific guidance is unverified.","UCAS English language tests page and admissions-tests page returned fetch errors; accepted tests listed above come from the UCAS 'tips for international applications' page.","How the Egyptian Baccalaureate (new system) is treated by UK universities: no opened page mentions it.","Whether SAT/ACT are used by any UK university for Egyptian applicants: not found on opened pages.","International-specific UCAS deadlines: UCAS states only that many universities accept international applications later; per-university dates not checked.","Whether Egyptian student visa applicants need a TB test: the gov.uk page does not list nationalities.","Undergraduate scholarships specifically for Egyptian students: none found on opened official pages (Manchester Egypt scholarships page not opened).","UCL English language requirement scores and any UCL Egypt-specific entry rule: not opened.","Tuition fees: only a general Study UK range (£11,400 to £30,000 a year) was seen on the Study UK page; per-university fees not checked.","UCAT test centre availability in Egypt: not verified.","Wording on Egypt in the final 22,000 characters of Oxford's international qualifications page and last 10,000 of Cambridge's entry page was not fully read; Oxford's 'Not accepted' status for Thanaweya A'ama was read in the first part of the page."],"flag":"🇬🇧"},"germany":{"id":"germany","name":"Germany","last_checked":"2026-10-13","cycle":"Winter semester 2026/27 has already started. Upcoming: summer semester 2027 (uni-assist says deadline is often 15 January) and winter semester 2027/28 (often 15 July). Exact deadlines vary by university and course; no university deadline page opened stated a year.","overview":"Germany has no single national application system for international undergraduates. Students apply either through uni-assist (which evaluates foreign certificates for about 180 universities) or directly to the university. Whether a foreign school certificate gives direct access, or requires first a Studienkolleg preparatory course or university study at home, depends on how the certificate is evaluated, and the university makes the final decision. Most programmes are taught in German; some are taught in English.","admission_model":"Programmes without admission restrictions allow direct enrolment if requirements are met; restricted programmes (nationwide or university-set) require an application. Applicants from outside the EU apply via uni-assist or directly, depending on the university. Some universities require a uni-assist preliminary review documentation (VPD) first (TUM and HAW Hamburg do). Heidelberg takes direct applications from international applicants and reserves 8-10% of places in admission-restricted programmes for international students. Applicants whose certificate is not recognised as a university entrance qualification (HZB) can attend a Studienkolleg and pass the Feststellungsprüfung (FSP).","tests":[{"name":"TestAS","policy":"Aptitude test for international applicants to undergraduate study in Germany; many universities use it and a good result 'can strengthen your application or even be a prerequisite'. DAAD calls it optional and says it can improve admission chances. The page lists next dates 26 Nov 2026, 25 Feb 2027, 18 Mar 2027. Fee and Egypt test centres were not stated on the page opened.","examples":[],"source":"https://www.testas.de/en/"},{"name":"Feststellungsprüfung (end of Studienkolleg)","policy":"Final assessment at the end of a Studienkolleg (usually two semesters; very strong students may finish in one). Passing it, combined with the foreign certificate, gives subject-specific access to university or university of applied sciences study. Course types: M (medical/biological/pharmaceutical), W (business/economics/social sciences), G (humanities), T (maths/science/technical), S (languages). Studienkolleg teaches German up to C1.","examples":[{"university":"Heidelberg University","statement":"Studienkolleg is for applicants whose foreign entrance qualification is only partly comparable to the Abitur; German at B2+ is required and a compulsory German entrance exam applies; a failed FSP can be retaken once at the same Studienkolleg.","source":"https://uni-heidelberg.de/en/study/application-enrolment/requirements-for-enrolment/preparatory-course-studienkolleg-and-assessment-test-feststellungsprufung"},{"university":"HAW Hamburg","statement":"Page says its Studienkolleg preparatory course was held for the last time in 2024 and asks applicants not to contact Studienkolleg Hamburg.","source":"https://www.haw-hamburg.de/en/study/applications/international-applicants/"}],"source":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/requirements/studienkollegs/"}],"english":[{"test":"English-taught programmes (general)","note":"DAAD says English-taught programmes do not require German but need proof of English proficiency; requirements vary by institution and programme. Even English-taught programmes may require basic German at some universities (HAW Hamburg notes this).","source":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/requirements/overview/"},{"test":"TUM (example, English-taught bachelor)","note":"As a rule proof of English is required before the end of the application period; only certificates on TUM's recognised list are accepted (the list was not readable on the page opened); school grades cannot prove English. Some bachelor programmes (e.g. Aerospace, Information Engineering, Management and Technology at Munich Campus) require no certificate and test English in the aptitude assessment.","source":"https://www.tum.de/en/studies/application/application-info-portal/admission-requirements/language-certificates"}],"german_language":[{"test":"DAAD general","note":"Most programmes are taught in German and typically require at least B2 (CEFR); proof via a recognised certificate or on-site test. Requirements vary by institution and programme.","source":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/requirements/overview/"},{"test":"HAW Hamburg (example list)","note":"Accepted: DSH 2 from a registered German university; TestDaF level 4 in all subtests; Goethe-Zertifikat C1/C2; telc C1 University; ÖSD C1; DSD II; others listed on the page.","source":"https://www.haw-hamburg.de/en/study/applications/international-applicants/language-skills/"},{"test":"Studienkolleg entry","note":"DAAD overview: Studienkolleg requires German at B1-B2 and an entrance exam; Heidelberg requires B2+.","source":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/requirements/overview/"}],"documents":[{"name":"Uni-assist application documents","note":"Scans of all required documents (certified translations may be needed); registration in the My assist portal; handling fee per application. The complete document list was not on the pages opened; uni-assist refers to its 'assemble your documents' section.","source":"https://www.uni-assist.de/en/"},{"name":"VPD (preliminary review documentation)","note":"Certificate from uni-assist for certain universities showing which certificates were evaluated and where grades fall in the German system; valid twelve months after issue; submitted to the university with other documents. TUM: a VPD application alone is not an application to TUM; Bachelor and Master VPDs are separate.","source":"https://www.uni-assist.de/en/how-to-apply/plan-your-application/vpd/"},{"name":"Language certificate","note":"German or English proof depending on programme.","source":"https://www.haw-hamburg.de/en/study/applications/international-applicants/"},{"name":"School certificate and transcript","note":"Heidelberg/TUM require authenticated copies of school records; TUM uploads them to TUMonline.","source":"https://www.tum.de/en/studies/application/application-info-portal/application-international"},{"name":"Study visa documents (German Embassy Cairo)","note":"Passport; VIDEX form; 2 biometric photos; health insurance (min. EUR 30,000 Schengen cover); CV; motivation letter; last school or university diploma with transcript, translated and legalised; admission letter (Zulassungsbescheid) from a university or Studienkolleg; language proof; financial proof; fee EUR 75. The document header says 'Stand: Mai 2022' but the body is marked 02/2025.","source":"https://kairo.diplo.de/resource/blob/2573898/c9d4d2346e89d959bf7b822ac5262751/231116-studium-englisch-data.pdf"}],"timeline":[{"when":"At least 12 months before intended start (during or before final school year)","step":"Check recognition of the Egyptian certificate (DAAD admission database / anabin / uni-assist) and each university's rules. Timing relative to the Egyptian school year is not given by any opened official page; this row is an inference from the dates below.","source":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/requirements/overview/"},{"when":"Before the application deadline (WS: often 15 July; SS: often 15 January)","step":"uni-assist: submit online application and complete documents before the deadline; apply at least 8 weeks before the deadline. Many universities set earlier deadlines for some courses or Studienkolleg.","source":"https://www.uni-assist.de/en/how-to-apply/plan-your-application/deadlines-processing-time/"},{"when":"After submitting to uni-assist","step":"Evaluation result usually in 4 to 6 weeks from receipt of the online form (page lists 2-3 weeks for Africa, Middle East and Iran; may take longer). Page last updated 28 September 2026.","source":"https://www.uni-assist.de/en/how-to-apply/plan-your-application/deadlines-processing-time/"},{"when":"If TestAS is wanted or required","step":"Upcoming TestAS dates: 26 Nov 2026, 25 Feb 2027, 18 Mar 2027.","source":"https://www.testas.de/en/"},{"when":"After admission (Zulassungsbescheid)","step":"Apply for the national study visa; the Cairo embassy states processing of about 4-5 weeks, it can take longer, and travel is no earlier than two weeks before the start of preparatory courses or lectures.","source":"https://kairo.diplo.de/resource/blob/2573898/c9d4d2346e89d959bf7b822ac5262751/231116-studium-englisch-data.pdf"},{"when":"Example university deadline","step":"Heidelberg: application period 1 June to 15 July for winter semester for non-EU applicants with foreign qualifications in the nationwide-restricted subjects (medicine, pharmacy, dentistry); no summer semester for those subjects. The year was not stated; other subjects' dates were not shown.","source":"https://www.uni-heidelberg.de/en/study/management-of-studies/key-dates-deadlines/application-deadlines-for-the-1st-semester-of-undergraduate-degree-programmes"}],"visa":{"summary":"Study visa (national visa): German Embassy Cairo document sheet requires proof of at least EUR 992 per month (EUR 11,904 per year) via a blocked account (Sperrkonto, opened before applying), a scholarship letter from an official German institution (e.g. DAAD, Erasmus), or a Verpflichtungserklärung. Language proof: B1 German certificate, or proof that the language of instruction was English (for English-taught studies), or registration for a German language course if necessary. Visa fee EUR 75. The Federal Foreign Office blocked-account page states no amount itself and says the amount depends on the purpose of stay and should be checked with the competent mission. Note: a germany.info page (US embassy) shows EUR 853 per month, which is outdated against the Cairo sheet; use the Cairo/Federal Foreign Office figure and re-check before applying.","source":"https://kairo.diplo.de/resource/blob/2573898/c9d4d2346e89d959bf7b822ac5262751/231116-studium-englisch-data.pdf"},"funding":[{"name":"DAAD scholarships overview","note":"DAAD pages opened say scholarships are aimed primarily at graduates and doctoral students (sentence partially cut off in the fetched text); no bachelor-level scholarship for international first-degree students was named.","url":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/scholarships/daad-scholarships/"},{"name":"DAAD scholarship database","note":"DAAD says international students can apply to numerous organisations and the scholarship database lists suitable offers; use it to check bachelor-level options.","url":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/scholarships/"},{"name":"DAAD Study scholarships for STEM disciplines","note":"Funds a Master's for graduates from developing and emerging countries; requires a completed first degree. Not for bachelor entry.","url":"https://www2.daad.de/deutschland/stipendium/datenbank/en/21148-scholarship-database/?detail=57742130"}],"egyptian_notes":[{"note":"uni-assist's Egypt page does not mention Thanaweya Amma, the General Secondary Education Certificate or the Egyptian Baccalaureate. It lists: private school diploma (ZAB evaluates; 1 year of accredited university study qualifies for Studienkolleg in the same subject area, 2 years for a bachelor in the same subject area); Al-Azhar school leaving certificate (documents listed, what it qualifies for not stated); Certificate of Nile International Secondary Education (qualifies for Studienkolleg; documents include enrolment certificate at an Egyptian university, Tansik Nomination Card and national exam certificates); and degrees from private Egyptian universities.","source":"https://www.uni-assist.de/en/tools/info-country-by-country/details-country/country/eg"},{"note":"DAAD says certificates from non-EU countries often require two or three semesters of comparable study at home or a Studienkolleg in Germany; recognition can be checked in the DAAD admission database, My GUIDE or anabin, and the institution decides. The DAAD admission database page opened says it covers about 140 countries but does not list them, so Egypt's entry could not be confirmed.","source":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/requirements/overview/"},{"note":"TUM: direct admission depends on equivalence of the foreign certificate; if not comparable, a Studienkolleg and the assessment exam are needed; some foreign qualifications only allow certain subjects. The TUM page does not mention Egypt.","source":"https://www.tum.de/en/studies/application/application-info-portal/higher-education-entrance-qualification/international-higher-education-entrance-qualification/"},{"note":"Heidelberg: foreign qualifications are assessed using the ZAB framework; anabin and DAAD are pointed to for checking recognition.","source":"https://uni-heidelberg.de/en/study/application-enrolment/requirements-for-enrolment/preparatory-course-studienkolleg-and-assessment-test-feststellungsprufung"}],"universities":[{"name":"Technical University of Munich (TUM)","country":"Germany","why_example":"Large technical university; VPD via uni-assist plus TUMonline application.","requirements":"VPD from uni-assist required for non-German qualifications; apply separately via TUMonline; direct admission only if certificate is equivalent, otherwise Studienkolleg; German or English proof depending on programme; semester periods WS 2026/27: 1 Oct 2026 - 31 Mar 2027 (application deadlines not readable on pages opened).","url":"https://www.tum.de/en/studies/application/application-info-portal/application-international"},{"name":"Heidelberg University","country":"Germany","why_example":"Comprehensive university with direct (not uni-assist) application for international bachelor applicants.","requirements":"Direct application via heiCO; 8-10% of places in restricted subjects for international students; very good German required; Studienkolleg route needs B2+ German; deadline for winter semester 1 June-15 July for nationwide-restricted subjects (year not stated).","url":"https://www.uni-heidelberg.de/en/study/application-enrolment/starting-the-first-academic-semester-of-your-degree-programme/internal-university-selection-procedure/internal-university-selection-procedure-0"},{"name":"HAW Hamburg (University of Applied Sciences)","country":"Germany","why_example":"University of applied sciences using uni-assist VPD with published language list.","requirements":"VPD from uni-assist (assessment up to 8 weeks); deadlines per course page; German: DSH 2, TestDaF 4 in all subtests, Goethe C1 etc.; page last changed 22.07.2026.","url":"https://www.haw-hamburg.de/en/study/applications/international-applicants/"}],"key_links":[{"label":"DAAD: requirements overview","url":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/requirements/overview/"},{"label":"DAAD: Studienkollegs","url":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/requirements/studienkollegs/"},{"label":"DAAD: admission requirements database","url":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/requirements/admission-database/"},{"label":"DAAD: scholarships","url":"https://www.daad.de/en/studying-in-germany/scholarships/"},{"label":"uni-assist","url":"https://www.uni-assist.de/en/"},{"label":"uni-assist: Egypt","url":"https://www.uni-assist.de/en/tools/info-country-by-country/details-country/country/eg"},{"label":"uni-assist: deadlines and processing time","url":"https://www.uni-assist.de/en/how-to-apply/plan-your-application/deadlines-processing-time/"},{"label":"TestAS","url":"https://www.testas.de/en/"},{"label":"Federal Foreign Office: blocked account","url":"https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/visa-service/visabestimmungen-node/sperrkonto-seite"},{"label":"German Embassy Cairo: study visa sheet (PDF)","url":"https://kairo.diplo.de/resource/blob/2573898/c9d4d2346e89d959bf7b822ac5262751/231116-studium-englisch-data.pdf"}],"unverified":["Study in Germany (study-in-germany.de) and the DAAD admission database results page (www2.daad.de) are blocked by robots restrictions; DAAD 'language skills' page also blocked. The DAAD database entry for Egypt could not be viewed.","Whether Thanaweya Amma holders may enter directly, need Studienkolleg, or need first-year university study in Egypt: no opened official page states this. The uni-assist Egypt page omits Thanaweya Amma. Anabin was not opened (German-language, not attempted).","Treatment of the Egyptian Baccalaureate: not mentioned on any opened page.","TestDaF official page returned a server error; TestDaF levels are only seen via the HAW Hamburg language page. DSH level 2 likewise via HAW Hamburg. IELTS/TOEFL scores for TUM were not readable.","TestAS fee, registration steps and Egyptian test centres: not stated on pages opened (TestAS registration pages could not be fetched).","TUM bachelor application deadlines (winter and summer) were not shown on pages opened; Heidelberg deadlines for programmes other than medicine/pharmacy/dentistry and the year were not shown; HAW Hamburg deadlines are per course.","uni-assist deadlines are described as 'often' 15 July and 15 January, and uni-assist says many universities set earlier dates; the full uni-assist document checklist was not opened.","Blocked account (Sperrkonto): the Federal Foreign Office page states no amount; the EUR 992/month figure is from the Cairo embassy PDF (dated Stand 02/2025 in the body, 'Mai 2022' in header); a germany.info page shows EUR 853, so confirm the current figure with the German Embassy Cairo.","Bachelor-level DAAD scholarships for Egyptians: none found on opened official pages; DAAD Cairo regional office pages (blog.daad.de/daad-egypt-alt) were found in search but not opened.","Typical timing relative to the Egyptian final school year (e.g. when Thanaweya Amma results arrive versus German deadlines): not stated on any official page; no recommendation given."],"flag":"🇩🇪"},"canada":{"id":"canada","name":"Canada","last_checked":"2026-10-13","overview":"Education is the responsibility of provincial and territorial governments (EduCanada). Students apply to each university; most international students then need a study permit from IRCC, which requires a letter of acceptance from a designated learning institution (DLI) and, for undergraduates outside Quebec, a provincial/territorial attestation letter (PAL/TAL) in most cases.","admission_model":"Direct application to each university. Ontario universities use the Ontario Universities' Application Centre (OUAC), per University of Toronto: apply via OUAC, then upload documents in the applicant portal. UBC applies through its own online application. Admission is based on academic record in your curriculum; requirements vary by program and university. Whether other provinces use central systems was not verified.","tests":[{"name":"SAT/ACT","policy":"Generally not a standard requirement for Canadian universities in the pages opened; University of Toronto says applicants with SAT/ACT 'may submit' scores for consideration (U.S.-curriculum section) and Engineering applicants must disclose all test scores. No SAT/ACT statement from UBC or Memorial found. Varies by university and program.","examples":[{"university":"University of Toronto","statement":"Applicants who have taken the SAT or ACT may submit scores for consideration (U.S.-patterned curriculum section); Engineering applicants must disclose all test scores.","source":"https://future.utoronto.ca/requirements-international-high-schools"}],"source":"https://future.utoronto.ca/requirements-international-high-schools"}],"english":[{"test":"UBC Vancouver (2027/2028 Winter Session)","note":"IELTS Academic 6.5 overall, no part below 6.0; TOEFL iBT 90 (Reading/Listening 22, Writing/Speaking 21) or new scale 4.5 overall; Duolingo 125 with sub-scores (Reading/Listening 115, Writing/Speaking 120). Single sitting only. IELTS General/Indicator not accepted. Proof deadline Feb 15.","source":"https://you.ubc.ca/applying-ubc/requirements/english-language-competency/"},{"test":"University of Toronto","note":"TOEFL iBT new scale: overall 4.5, Writing 4.5, Speaking 4.0 (89 total for tests before Jan 21 2026); IELTS Academic overall 6.5 with no band below 6.0; Duolingo 120 overall and 120 Production (tests on/after July 1 2024). Same-date scores; MyBest and IELTS One Skill Retake not accepted. Egypt not listed among exemption countries.","source":"https://future.utoronto.ca/english-language-requirements"},{"test":"Memorial University","note":"For Egyptian General Secondary Education Certificate applicants: proof of English proficiency through a standardized test is required (minimum scores not seen).","source":"https://www.mun.ca/undergrad/admissions/i-want-to-apply/international-high-school-curriculum-requirements/egypt/"}],"documents":[{"name":"Academic transcripts","note":"U of T: after applying, the applicant portal shows a personalized list of required documents. Laurier (Thanaweya Amma): transcripts grades 9-12 sent from Ministry of Education or Regional Governorate; final official transcript to clear conditions.","source":"https://www.wlu.ca/future-students/undergraduate/admissions/assets/resources/requirements-by-country/africa/egypt.html"},{"name":"Letter of acceptance","note":"Always required for study permit; validated by school for post-secondary.","source":"https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/study-permit/get-documents.html"},{"name":"PAL/TAL","note":"Needed in most cases outside Quebec (Quebec: CAQ). Undergraduate is not exempt; 2026 PALs valid to Dec 31, 2026 only (cap year).","source":"https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/study-permit/get-documents/provincial-attestation-letter.html"},{"name":"Passport and photos","note":"Valid passport; two passport-size photos with name and DOB on back.","source":"https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/study-permit/get-documents.html"},{"name":"Proof of funds","note":"Always required.","source":"https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/study-permit/get-documents/financial-support.html"},{"name":"Letter of explanation, medical exam, police certificate","note":"Letter recommended; medical/police only if required; requirements vary by visa office.","source":"https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/study-permit/get-documents.html"}],"timeline":[{"when":"Early October of final school year","step":"UBC international applications open (for Winter Session Sept 2027); UBC award deadline Nov 15 2026 for International Scholars Program.","source":"https://you.ubc.ca/applying-ubc/dates-deadlines/"},{"when":"November 7 (recommended) of final school year","step":"U of T recommended early application date (2027 admissions), document submission by Dec 1 for early consideration.","source":"https://future.utoronto.ca/deadlines"},{"when":"January 15 of final school year","step":"UBC general deadline (Jan 15 2027) and U of T deadline for most programs (Jan 15, 2027 admissions). Some U of T programs: Feb 1.","source":"https://you.ubc.ca/applying-ubc/dates-deadlines/"},{"when":"Jan 31 - Mar 15","step":"UBC: English proof by Feb 15; documents by Mar 15 for outside-Canada high school applicants; International Scholars docs by Jan 31.","source":"https://you.ubc.ca/applying-ubc/dates-deadlines/"},{"when":"January to late May","step":"U of T admission decisions released beginning January through late May.","source":"https://future.utoronto.ca/deadlines"},{"when":"May 1 or June 1","step":"UBC deadline to accept offer and pay deposit; then apply for study permit as soon as you accept (processing can take several months, per UBC).","source":"https://you.ubc.ca/applying-ubc/dates-deadlines/"},{"when":"July-August","step":"UBC final transcript deadline July 25 2027 for out-of-country high school applicants.","source":"https://you.ubc.ca/applying-ubc/dates-deadlines/"}],"visa":{"summary":"Study permit fee CAD 150; apply before travelling; processing time varies by country (IRCC tool). Living-cost funds excluding tuition and transport for one applicant outside Quebec: CAD 22,895/year for applications Jan 1 2025 to Aug 31 2026; CAD 23,448/year for applications on or after Sep 1 2026. Also show first-year tuition and housing funds and travel costs. Quebec amounts set by Quebec ministry (not verified).","source":"https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/study-permit/get-documents/financial-support.html"},"funding":[{"name":"UBC International Major Entrance Scholarship and Outstanding International Student Award","note":"Automatic consideration if you apply by the admission deadline; IMES CAD 10,000-25,000 per year for 2026/2027, renewable; OIS one-time CAD 10,000-25,000 (2025/2026 value).","url":"https://you.ubc.ca/financial-planning/scholarships-awards-international-students/"},{"name":"UBC International Scholars Program","note":"Need-and-merit, nomination required; apply by Nov 15 2026 for Sept 2027 entry.","url":"https://you.ubc.ca/financial-planning/scholarships-awards-international-students/international-scholars/"},{"name":"University of Toronto Lester B. Pearson International Scholarships","note":"About 37 recipients each year; covers tuition, books, incidental fees and residence for four years.","url":"https://future.utoronto.ca/international-students"},{"name":"EduCanada scholarships page","note":"Official portal; no undergraduate programs named on the page opened.","url":"https://www.educanada.ca/scholarships-bourses/index.aspx?lang=eng"}],"egyptian_notes":[{"note":"Memorial University accepts the General Secondary Education Certificate: required English, mathematics, a lab science, social studies or language, and one elective; minimum 65% average in required subjects at senior level; English test required; competitive programs may need higher.","source":"https://www.mun.ca/undergrad/admissions/i-want-to-apply/international-high-school-curriculum-requirements/egypt/"},{"note":"Wilfrid Laurier University lists Thanaweya a'Amma: six academic courses, transcripts grades 9-12 from Ministry of Education or Governorate, final transcript to clear conditions.","source":"https://www.wlu.ca/future-students/undergraduate/admissions/assets/resources/requirements-by-country/africa/egypt.html"},{"note":"UBC lists 'Egypt - 11 Years of Education' and 'Egypt - 12 Years of Education' in its country selector; details not retrieved. Its general catch-all for other systems requires a university-preparation program within a 12-year system.","source":"https://you.ubc.ca/applying-ubc/requirements/international-high-schools/"}],"universities":[{"name":"University of Toronto","country":"Canada","why_example":"Highly selective public, OUAC applicant","requirements":"Apply via OUAC; senior-level English plus program prerequisites; English test (IELTS 6.5/TOEFL new 4.5/Duolingo 120). 2027 deadline Jan 15 for most programs, Nov 7 recommended; documents Feb 1.","url":"https://future.utoronto.ca/international-students"},{"name":"University of British Columbia (Vancouver)","country":"Canada","why_example":"Large public, automatic merit scholarship consideration","requirements":"English: IELTS 6.5, TOEFL iBT 90, Duolingo 125. Deadline Jan 15 2027 for Sept 2027; documents by Mar 15 for non-Canadian high school applicants.","url":"https://you.ubc.ca/applying-ubc/dates-deadlines/"},{"name":"Memorial University of Newfoundland","country":"Canada","why_example":"Mid-size public with Egypt-specific page","requirements":"Egyptian General Secondary Education Certificate with minimum 65% average in required subjects; English test required. Deadlines not verified.","url":"https://www.mun.ca/undergrad/admissions/i-want-to-apply/international-high-school-curriculum-requirements/egypt/"}],"key_links":[{"label":"IRCC: study permit","url":"https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/study-permit.html"},{"label":"IRCC: documents","url":"https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/study-permit/get-documents.html"},{"label":"IRCC: proof of funds","url":"https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/study-canada/study-permit/get-documents/financial-support.html"},{"label":"EduCanada: study in Canada","url":"https://www.educanada.ca/study-plan-etudes/index.aspx?lang=eng"},{"label":"EduCanada: scholarships","url":"https://www.educanada.ca/scholarships-bourses/index.aspx?lang=eng"},{"label":"EduCanada: education system","url":"https://www.educanada.ca/study-plan-etudes/system-education-systeme.aspx?lang=eng"}],"unverified":["OUAC pages blocked by robots (ouac.on.ca); OUAC use confirmed only via U of T statement","UBC Egypt requirement details (dropdown only); UBC page on international high schools content blank","Egyptian Baccalaureate recognition: not found on any page","U of T Egypt page not opened (high-school-by-country page not fetched)","Memorial and other universities' deadlines","SAT/ACT stance at UBC and Memorial","Quebec CAQ requirements and amounts","Processing time for Egyptian applicants (IRCC tool not opened)","IRCC Egypt visa office specifics (how-to-apply page not opened)","Whether PAL allocations for the 2027 cap year are published","Federal undergraduate scholarship for Egyptians (none identified)"],"flag":"🇨🇦"},"turkey":{"id":"turkey","name":"Turkey","last_checked":"2026-10-13","overview":"International undergraduate applicants to Turkiye can apply to individual universities (each sets its own documents, exams and dates) or to the government Turkiye Burslari scholarship. Study in Turkiye lists a 5-step route: choose programme, check scholarships, prepare documents, check exam requirements, then apply for a student visa after admission. Cycle status as of 2026-10-13: the 2026-27 intake application windows seen (ITU, Bilkent, Turkiye Burslari 2026) have already closed; dates for the 2027-28 intake were not found on pages opened.","admission_model":"Decentralised: each university publishes its own international-student admission conditions. Study in Turkiye says an entrance exam, language score or skill test may be required, that some universities accept scores from exams taken in the applicant's country and others run their own exams, and names TR-YOS (run by OSYM) as an exam for international candidates. Turkiye Burslari is a separate, competitive, merit-based government scholarship applied for online, free of charge.","tests":[{"name":"TR-YOS (OSYM exam for foreign students)","policy":"Study in Turkiye states TR-YOS is held twice a year by OSYM, offered in Turkish, German, Arabic, French, English and Russian, at centres in Turkiye and abroad, with no Turkish skills needed. It states Turkish public and foundation universities require TR-YOS scores. Policy still varies: ITU and Bilkent pages opened list other accepted scores (see examples). 2026-TR-YOS/2 was held 11 October 2026 (applications 9 July to 3 August 2026). 2027 dates not found.","examples":[{"university":"OSYM","statement":"2026 TR-YOS/2 administered by OSYM on October 11, 2026; applications July 9 to August 3, 2026. Page does not mention exam centres or Egypt.","source":"https://en.osym.gov.tr/applications-for-2026-exam-for-foreign-students-for-higher-education-in-turkiye-2026-tr-yos2"}],"source":"https://studyinturkiye.gov.tr/StudyinTurkey/StudyinTurkeyTRYOS"},{"name":"SAT and other international qualifications (university-specific)","policy":"Accepted only where the individual university lists them. Bilkent (2026-27 fall intake) lists SAT, A Level, IB and olympiad medals; its page does not mention YOS or Egyptian qualifications directly.","examples":[{"university":"Bilkent University","statement":"SAT Reasoning: minimum 1000/1600 in Math and Critical Reading; SAT Subject: minimum 500/800 in at least two program-related sections; A Level: three subjects at C or higher; IB: minimum 28/45 with a relevant HL subject. Predicted grades/results are not evaluated. Applications 2 February to 12 July 2026 (2026-27 fall).","source":"https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/international/how-to-apply/"},{"university":"Istanbul Technical University (ITU)","statement":"Application only with exam/diploma scores in its Article B (valid exams) list; lower scores not accepted; meeting minimums does not guarantee admission. The Article B list was blank in the page version opened, so ITU's accepted exams are unverified.","source":"https://www.sis.itu.edu.tr/duyuru_ekler/yabanci/202710/EN/index.php"}],"source":"https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/international/how-to-apply/"}],"english":[{"test":"ITU English proficiency","note":"ITU requires an accepted English proficiency result at registration; without it, a one-year English preparatory course at its College of Foreign Language. Accepted tests and scores are on a separate ITU page not opened. Programmes taught at least 30% in English require a C1 Turkish certificate within one year of registration (from ITU TOMER or Yunus Emre Institutes).","source":"https://www.sis.itu.edu.tr/duyuru_ekler/yabanci/202710/EN/index.php"},{"test":"Bilkent English proficiency","note":"Not stated on the how-to-apply page; Bilkent refers to a separate English Language Proficiency page that was not opened.","source":"https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/international/how-to-apply/"}],"documents":[{"name":"High school diploma with equivalency certificate (ITU)","note":"ITU asks for the diploma with an Equivalency Certificate showing it matches a Turkish high school diploma; applicants still in school provide proof of expected graduation date. Documents not in Turkish or English need certified translation.","source":"https://www.sis.itu.edu.tr/duyuru_ekler/yabanci/202710/EN/index.php"},{"name":"Official transcript","note":"ITU: all courses and grades, approved by the high school.","source":"https://www.sis.itu.edu.tr/EN/student/intenational-students/application.php"},{"name":"Valid exam result","note":"ITU: original valid test report; certified translation if not in Turkish or English.","source":"https://www.sis.itu.edu.tr/EN/student/intenational-students/application.php"},{"name":"Passport copy","note":"ITU: identification page; national ID accepted if no passport. Files uploaded as PDF, up to 2 MB each (2026-27 page).","source":"https://www.sis.itu.edu.tr/duyuru_ekler/yabanci/202710/EN/index.php"},{"name":"Statement of purpose","note":"ITU 2026-27 page lists a 300-word statement; the general ITU application page says it applies only to the Textile Development and Marketing programme. Treat as programme-specific; check the current page.","source":"https://www.sis.itu.edu.tr/duyuru_ekler/yabanci/202710/EN/index.php"},{"name":"Originals on admission (Bilkent)","note":"Admitted students must provide originals of all submitted documents; Bilkent may verify exam scores.","source":"https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/international/how-to-apply/"},{"name":"Documents vary by university","note":"Study in Turkiye: required documents vary by university and programme; check the programme page.","source":"https://studyinturkiye.gov.tr/"}],"timeline":[{"when":"Final school year, roughly Jan to Feb (Turkiye Burslari)","step":"Turkiye Burslari general application period shown on official calendar as January 10 to February 20, results early August. The calendar page does not state a year. The 2026 cycle was announced by YTB as January 10 to February 20, 2026 (closed). 2027 dates not found.","source":"https://www.turkiyeburslari.gov.tr/calendar"},{"when":"Final school year, roughly Feb to mid-July (university applications, 2026-27 examples)","step":"Bilkent accepted applications 2 February to 12 July 2026; ITU 18 May to 17 July 2026 with admissions announced 27 July 2026. Dates differ by university and year; 2027-28 dates not found.","source":"https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/international/how-to-apply/"},{"when":"Final school year, exam sitting","step":"TR-YOS is held twice a year; 2026 TR-YOS/2 was on 11 October 2026 (applications 9 July to 3 August).","source":"https://en.osym.gov.tr/applications-for-2026-exam-for-foreign-students-for-higher-education-in-turkiye-2026-tr-yos2"},{"when":"After admission letter","step":"Apply for student visa at nearest Turkish consulate as soon as the admission letter is received; then submit residence permit documents early via the university.","source":"https://studyinturkiye.gov.tr/StudyinTurkey/ShowDetail?rID=Egqvn0o1tiU=&&cId=PE4Nr0mMoY4="}],"visa":{"summary":"Study in Turkiye: students must obtain a student visa from the nearest Turkish consulate; processing can take time, so apply as soon as the admission letter arrives; check requirements for your nationality on the Ministry of Foreign Affairs site; online application via konsolosluk.gov.tr. Residence permit: under a protocol effective 29 November 2023, higher-education students should submit residence permit documents early to their university's student/international office; checklist is on goc.gov.tr (not opened).","source":"https://studyinturkiye.gov.tr/StudyinTurkey/ShowDetail?rID=Egqvn0o1tiU=&&cId=PE4Nr0mMoY4="},"funding":[{"name":"Turkiye Burslari (Turkiye Scholarships), YTB","note":"Competitive, merit-based government scholarship; online application, free of charge. 2026 applications ran January 10 to February 20, 2026 (closed). Level covered includes associate and undergraduate. The official archived criteria page (dated 2021 content) lists: under 21 for undergraduate, minimum 70% academic achievement, citizens of all countries except holders/renouncers of Turkish nationality. These criteria are from an old cycle; confirm on the current site before relying on them.","url":"https://www.ytb.gov.tr/en/news/turkiye-scholarships-2026-applications-are-now-open"},{"name":"University scholarships","note":"Study in Turkiye: offers vary by institution; check each university's website.","url":"https://studyinturkiye.gov.tr/"}],"egyptian_notes":[{"note":"No page opened mentions Egypt, Thanaweya Amma or the Egyptian Baccalaureate for Turkish admission. Bilkent says a separate PDF lists minimum scores for national qualifications (not opened).","source":"https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/international/how-to-apply/"},{"note":"ITU requires an equivalency certificate for the high school diploma (issuing body not named on the page opened).","source":"https://www.sis.itu.edu.tr/EN/student/intenational-students/application.php"}],"universities":[{"name":"Istanbul Technical University (ITU)","country":"Turkey","why_example":"Public technical university; uses a valid-exam list plus equivalency-certified diploma.","requirements":"2026-27: apply 18 May to 17 July 2026; diploma with equivalency certificate, transcript, valid test report, passport copy; English test or one-year prep; C1 Turkish for 30%-English programmes. Accepted-exam list not visible on page opened.","url":"https://www.sis.itu.edu.tr/EN/student/intenational-students/application.php"},{"name":"Bilkent University","country":"Turkey","why_example":"Private (foundation) university using SAT/A Level/IB thresholds instead of a YOS-only route.","requirements":"2026-27 fall: applications 2 February to 12 July 2026; SAT 1000/1600 (Math + Critical Reading) or A Level/IB/olympiad options; predicted results not evaluated.","url":"https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/international/how-to-apply/"}],"key_links":[{"label":"Study in Turkiye (official)","url":"https://studyinturkiye.gov.tr/"},{"label":"Study in Turkiye - TR-YOS","url":"https://studyinturkiye.gov.tr/StudyinTurkey/StudyinTurkeyTRYOS"},{"label":"Study in Turkiye - Visa and Residence","url":"https://studyinturkiye.gov.tr/StudyinTurkey/ShowDetail?rID=Egqvn0o1tiU=&&cId=PE4Nr0mMoY4="},{"label":"Study in Turkiye - Recognition and Equivalence (degrees only)","url":"https://studyinturkiye.gov.tr/StudyinTurkey/ShowDetail?rID=7kfKef+q+vg=&&cId=PE4Nr0mMoY4="},{"label":"Turkiye Burslari","url":"https://turkiyeburslari.gov.tr/en"},{"label":"Turkiye Burslari calendar","url":"https://www.turkiyeburslari.gov.tr/calendar"},{"label":"OSYM (English)","url":"https://en.osym.gov.tr/"}],"unverified":["Dates for the 2027-28 intake (Turkiye Burslari 2027, TR-YOS 2027, ITU, Bilkent): not published on pages opened.","Current Turkiye Burslari undergraduate eligibility (age, minimum grade): only an archived page with 2021-era content was opened; current criteria page was not opened.","ITU accepted exams (Article B) and English score table: blank or not opened.","Bilkent English proficiency requirement and its list of national qualifications (Egypt): pages/PDF not opened.","YOK/CoHE recognition of high school diplomas: Study in Turkiye recognition page covers only associate, bachelor and master degrees, not secondary certificates.","Thanaweya Amma and Egyptian Baccalaureate acceptance by Turkish universities: no official statement found.","TR-YOS exam centres in Egypt, fees and score validity: not stated on pages opened; TR-YOS guide PDF not opened.","Third example Turkish university: only two (ITU, Bilkent) were verified before rate limits.","Whether TR-YOS is mandatory at every university: Study in Turkiye says public and foundation universities require TR-YOS scores, but ITU and Bilkent pages list other accepted exams; treat as varying."],"flag":"🇹🇷"},"uae":{"id":"uae","name":"United Arab Emirates","last_checked":"2026-10-13","overview":"Each UAE university sets its own international admission rules. Most pages opened require a secondary certificate attested through the home-country chain and an equivalency certificate from the UAE Ministry of Education for certificates issued outside the UAE; unattested scans are generally accepted to start, with attested originals before enrolment. Cycle: no page opened gave a dated 2026-27 or 2027-28 deadline, so cycle status is unverified for each university.","admission_model":"Direct application to each university. The u.ae portal says the Ministry of Higher Education and Scientific Research (MoHESR) licenses and accredits private institutions, runs a National Unified Registration System for Emirati students (not international students), and offers a University Qualifications Recognition service for qualifications from accredited institutions outside the UAE (that service concerns degrees, not school certificates). Equivalency of school certificates is done through the UAE Ministry of Education (moe.gov.ae) per AUS, Ajman University and Khalifa University pages.","tests":[{"name":"EmSAT","policy":"Not a universal requirement. Khalifa University states EmSAT is not mandatory (scores under 18 months old can be considered). AUS lists EmSAT Achieve English 1550 only as an English option for transfer applicants.","examples":[{"university":"Khalifa University","statement":"EmSAT is not mandatory; SAT Math 700 or higher may be considered subject to committee approval.","source":"https://www.ku.ac.ae/undergraduate-admission-faqs"},{"university":"American University of Sharjah","statement":"EmSAT Achieve English (1550) is an English-test option only for transfer applicants; Thanaweya Amma applicants are not stated to need SAT.","source":"https://www.aus.edu/admissions/bachelors-degrees/application-requirements"}],"source":"https://www.ku.ac.ae/undergraduate-admission-faqs"},{"name":"SAT","policy":"AUS: required only for American High School Diploma applicants (SAT Math at least 450). Khalifa: SAT Math 700+ may be considered.","examples":[{"university":"American University of Sharjah","statement":"SAT is required only for applicants with an American High School Diploma (including SABIS); SAT Math 450 or above.","source":"https://www.aus.edu/admissions/bachelors-degrees/application-requirements"}],"source":"https://www.aus.edu/admissions/bachelors-degrees/application-requirements"}],"english":[{"test":"AUS","note":"Only TOEFL and IELTS accepted. IELTS Academic 6.5; TOEFL iTP 550; TOEFL iBT shown inconsistently on the page (80 in documents list, 4.5 'previously 80' in table), so confirm with admissions. Reports valid two calendar years.","source":"https://www.aus.edu/admissions/bachelors-degrees/application-requirements"},{"test":"Khalifa University","note":"Academic IELTS 6.0 or TOEFL iBT 79; the higher of the two is used.","source":"https://www.ku.ac.ae/undergraduate-admission-faqs"},{"test":"Ajman University","note":"English-taught programmes: 80% in Grade 12 English or equivalent (IELTS Academic 5.0; TOEFL ITP 500 / iBT 61). Doctor of Medicine: IELTS 6.0.","source":"https://www.ajman.ac.ae/en/admissions/undergraduate/international-students"}],"documents":[{"name":"Secondary certificate and grade reports","note":"AUS: official secondary certificate and official grade reports for the last three secondary classes, letter of good conduct, passport scan, photo, English score, equivalency certificate. Application fee AED 400 plus 5% VAT.","source":"https://www.aus.edu/admissions/bachelors-degrees/application-requirements"},{"name":"Attestation of certificates","note":"AUS and Ajman: certificates from outside the UAE must be attested by the home educational authority, the home foreign ministry and the UAE Embassy. Unattested scans accepted to apply; attested originals required before enrolment.","source":"https://www.ajman.ac.ae/en/admissions/undergraduate/international-students"},{"name":"Equivalency certificate (UAE Ministry of Education)","note":"AUS: apply online via moe.gov.ae at least two months before first day of class; pending equivalency allows registration under a Conditional Admission Contract. Ajman: conditional admission letter from the Ministry. Khalifa: required for private/international school graduates; a No Objection Letter from MOE allows starting classes while pending.","source":"https://www.aus.edu/admissions/bachelors-degrees/application-requirements"},{"name":"Other documents (Ajman)","note":"Ajman notes medical reports from outside the UAE are not accepted and admissions may request additional documents.","source":"https://www.ajman.ac.ae/en/admissions/undergraduate/international-students"}],"timeline":[{"when":"Final school year (before certificate issued)","step":"AUS offers early admission to final-year Thanawya Ammah students on official grade reports for grades 10 and 11; final only after certified certificate is submitted. Khalifa lets applicants graduating with predicted results apply with most recent transcript. The AUS Thanawya page is undated.","source":"https://infodesk.aus.edu/hc/en-us/articles/115008647787-Thanawya-Ammah-Curriculum"},{"when":"At least 2 months before first day of class","step":"Apply for UAE MOE equivalency (AUS).","source":"https://www.aus.edu/admissions/bachelors-degrees/application-requirements"},{"when":"After applying","step":"Khalifa: admission decisions usually take 4 to 6 weeks after all required steps are completed. No intake deadlines stated on the page.","source":"https://www.ku.ac.ae/undergraduate-admission-faqs"}],"visa":{"summary":"u.ae: a student can be on the residence visa sponsored by a UAE-resident parent, or sponsored by the accredited university or college. Requires a certificate from the institution stating the study period and general residence visa provisions; universities help with the process. Applications go through the ICP service page. Parent sponsorship of sons is stated up to age 25 (older males must show enrolment). Pre-arrival entry/visa rules for Egyptian nationals were not opened.","source":"https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/visa-and-emirates-id/Types-of-visas/residence-visa-for-studying-in-the-uae"},"funding":[{"name":"University-specific scholarships","note":"Not verified from official pages for international applicants beyond: UAEU states international Veterinary Medicine students are admitted only with scholarships. No UAE university scholarship terms for Egyptians were opened.","url":"https://www.uaeu.ac.ae/en/admission/undergraduate-admissions-current-student.shtml"}],"egyptian_notes":[{"note":"AUS (undated page): Thanawya Ammah applicants need minimum 85% average in best two years or the final public exam; higher for some majors; required-subject grade B for engineering, science, architecture, interior design and business; UAE MOE equivalency required; English options listed there include IELTS 6.5, TOEFL iBT 80, iTP 550, EmSAT English 1550. The AUS requirements page (also undated) lists Thanaweya Amma and Applied Technology under General Secondary with 85% and equivalency, but shows IELTS/TOEFL only and EmSAT for transfers; the two AUS pages differ on EmSAT, so confirm.","source":"https://infodesk.aus.edu/hc/en-us/articles/115008647787-Thanawya-Ammah-Curriculum"},{"note":"AUS requirements page: Egyptian certificates are earned outside the UAE, so a UAE MOE Certificate of Equivalency is needed.","source":"https://www.aus.edu/admissions/bachelors-degrees/application-requirements"},{"note":"Khalifa University and Ajman University pages opened do not mention Egypt or Thanaweya Amma.","source":"https://www.ku.ac.ae/undergraduate-admission-faqs"}],"universities":[{"name":"American University of Sharjah (AUS)","country":"United Arab Emirates","why_example":"Explicit Thanawya Ammah guidance and attestation/equivalency steps.","requirements":"Thanaweya Amma: 85% (higher for some majors), MOE equivalency, IELTS 6.5 / TOEFL iTP 550; SAT only for American diploma; fee AED 400 plus VAT.","url":"https://www.aus.edu/admissions/bachelors-degrees/application-requirements"},{"name":"Khalifa University","country":"United Arab Emirates","why_example":"Science and engineering focus; EmSAT optional; IELTS 6.0 / TOEFL 79.","requirements":"Academic IELTS 6.0 or TOEFL iBT 79; EmSAT not mandatory; SAT Math 700+ may be considered; MOE equivalency for private/international school graduates; decisions in 4 to 6 weeks.","url":"https://www.ku.ac.ae/undergraduate-admission-faqs"},{"name":"Ajman University","country":"United Arab Emirates","why_example":"Lower English thresholds and clearly stated attestation chain; no EmSAT/SAT requirement stated on page.","requirements":"80% Grade 12 English or IELTS 5.0 / TOEFL iBT 61; attested certificate (home authority, foreign ministry, UAE Embassy) before enrolment; MOE equivalency or conditional admission letter.","url":"https://www.ajman.ac.ae/en/admissions/undergraduate/international-students"}],"key_links":[{"label":"u.ae - Higher education","url":"https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/education/higher-education"},{"label":"u.ae - Student admission and qualification recognition","url":"https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/education/higher-education/Student-admission-and-qualification-recognition"},{"label":"u.ae - Find higher education institutes","url":"https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/education/higher-education/find-higher-education-institutes-in-the-uae"},{"label":"u.ae - Residence visa for studying","url":"https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/visa-and-emirates-id/Types-of-visas/residence-visa-for-studying-in-the-uae"},{"label":"MoHESR","url":"https://www.mohesr.gov.ae"}],"unverified":["Dated deadlines and intake cycles for 2026-27 / 2027-28: AUS deadlines page and Ajman/Khalifa dates not obtained (AUS deadlines page hit a rate limit).","UAE Ministry of Education equivalency process page itself (fees, timing, Egypt-specific steps): not opened; only university descriptions seen.","Whether the MoHESR/Study in the UAE portal states a federal-level minimum for international applicants: u.ae pages opened cover only Emirati registration; MoHESR Admission Criteria PDFs found are per-institution and were not treated as general rules.","UAEU international requirements: the UAEU international PDF opened is for academic year 2016/2017 (outdated) and the current page covers UAE nationals; international requirements not verified.","Egyptian Baccalaureate acceptance: no official statement found.","Egypt-specific entry visa rules and student visa fees for Egyptian nationals: not opened.","UAE university scholarship terms for international applicants: not verified from official pages.","Note: AUS Thanawya Ammah page and AUS requirements page differ on EmSAT and TOEFL iBT figures; both undated."],"flag":"🇦🇪"}};
const PATH_EGYPT = {"last_checked":"2026-10-14","systems":[{"id":"thanaweya-amma","name":"Thanaweya Amma (General Secondary Education Certificate)","name_ar":"الثانوية العامة","summary":"Egypt's traditional national certificate for completing general secondary education, issued by the Egyptian government. Official Egyptian pages in 2026 refer to it alongside the Egyptian Baccalaureate.","structure":"Partly confirmed. The Ministry says the Baccalaureate shares its subjects and examination system with the General Secondary certificate, except third-year advanced-level specialised subjects (differing by no more than 20%). Third-year General Secondary students sit a first mandatory free exam in June and an optional second attempt in August (EGP 200 per subject) per a 2026-09-08 Cairo governorate page. Grade-year counting (which years count toward the total) not confirmed from an official source.","grading":"Not confirmed from an Egyptian official page. A Swiss university (Basel) lists entry as 'Thanaweya a'Amma (GSEC)' requiring an 80% average, which shows results are percentage-based, but this is a foreign university rule, not an Egyptian statement. Cairo governorate page (2026-08-03) says the Baccalaureate overall score is used under the same coordination (admission) system as Thanaweya Amma, with the same percentage thresholds.","tracks":["Not confirmed from an official source (scientific/literary branches not verified)"],"sources":["https://cairo.gov.eg/en/news/2026/septemper/8/a9e62061cb52415fb12c072e04388db3","https://cairo.gov.eg/en/news/2026/august/3/education/","https://moe.gov.eg/en/what-s-on/news/31-8-25","https://www.unibas.ch/dam/jcr:6356e4e7-d6e5-4982-a935-27230134d796/Laenderliste_auslaendische_Vorbildungsausweise_akademisches_Jahr_2026_2027_mit%20Links_pdf.2026-01-19-10-04-18.pdf"]},{"id":"egyptian-bac","name":"Egyptian Baccalaureate","name_ar":"البكالوريا المصرية","summary":"Official national certificate for completing general secondary education, issued by the Egyptian government like Thanaweya Amma (Cairo governorate page citing the Ministry, 2026-08-03). Announced to cabinet on 8 January 2025 (per AACRAO, a professional association, dated 2025-03-20). The Ministry signed a cooperation agreement with the International Baccalaureate Organization to review curricula and align with international benchmarks.","structure":"Ministry pages: 7 subjects over two academic years; general subjects in the first secondary year; specialisation from the second year in four tracks; students may switch tracks by changing two subjects; all take Arabic, a first foreign language, Egyptian history, religious education (needs 70% to pass, excluded from total) plus three track subjects. Two exam chances per year (second-year: May mandatory free, July optional EGP 200 per subject; third-year: June mandatory free, August optional EGP 200 per subject). From 2026/2027 students need 60% of weekly/monthly assessments to sit the first exam (2027/2028 for the third-year certificate details). Shares subjects with General Secondary, except third-year advanced subjects differing by at most 20%; one shared examination system.","grading":"Overall score; for university admission the same coordination system and same percentage thresholds as Thanaweya Amma apply, with no increase or decrease in the percentage (Cairo governorate page, 2026-08-03). Full scoring scale not confirmed.","tracks":["Medicine and Life Sciences","Engineering and Computer Science","Business","Arts and Literature"],"sources":["https://moe.gov.eg/en/what-s-on/news/baccalau","https://moe.gov.eg/en/what-s-on/news/house-of-rep-3","https://moe.gov.eg/en/what-s-on/news/31-8-25","https://cairo.gov.eg/en/news/2026/august/3/education/","https://cairo.gov.eg/en/news/2026/septemper/8/a9e62061cb52415fb12c072e04388db3","https://www.aacrao.org/edge/emergent-news/egypt-introduces-baccalaureate-certificate-system-as-alternative-to-thanaweya-amma"]}],"paperwork":[{"name":"Apostille Convention status of Egypt","note":"Egypt does not appear in the HCCH status table for the 1961 Apostille Convention (states beginning with E listed: Ecuador, El Salvador, Estonia, Eswatini only). Opened via a fetch tool that summarised the page; the HCCH table itself was read, not an Egyptian page.","country":"All","source":"https://www.hcch.net/en/instruments/conventions/status-table/?cid=41"},{"name":"Egypt not an Apostille signatory (Government of Canada)","note":"Canada's Cairo embassy page says: 'Since Egypt is not one of the signatory countries of the Apostille Convention' Canadian documents for Egypt need authentication by the Egyptian embassy/consulate and then legalisation by the legalization office of the Egyptian Ministry of Foreign Affairs. This describes Canadian documents going to Egypt, not Egyptian certificates going to Canada.","country":"Canada","source":"https://international.gc.ca/country-pays/egypt-egypte/cairo-caire-info.aspx?lang=eng"},{"name":"Egyptian documents: legalisation chain required by the Netherlands","note":"Egyptian document is legalised by the Egyptian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, then by the Dutch embassy in Cairo (online appointment, usually one working day). Arabic documents must be translated by a sworn translator into Dutch, English, French or German; page says to use a government translation office in Egypt. Alternative: legalise original in Egypt first, then have a sworn translator in the Netherlands translate it without legalising the translation. Page is about Egyptian documents in general, not school certificates specifically; it does not mention an Education Ministry step or apostille.","country":"All","source":"https://netherlandsworldwide.nl/legalisation/foreign-documents/egypt"},{"name":"Egyptian documents: legalisation required by Belgium","note":"Sworn translation into French, Dutch or German; legalisation by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in Egypt; then Belgian embassy legalisation via TLScontact; document must not be older than six months. Only the Foreign Ministry is named as the Egyptian step. Page does not state whether Egypt is in the Apostille Convention.","country":"All","source":"https://egypt.diplomatie.belgium.be/en/legalisation-documents"},{"name":"Egyptian documents: legalisation required by Finland","note":"Egyptian Ministry of Foreign Affairs confirms the local official's signature; the Finnish embassy in Cairo checks it against signature samples and legalises with a seal. The ministry certifies signatures only, not content. Page is about documents from local authorities (notary, court, registry), not school certificates.","country":"All","source":"https://finlandabroad.fi/web/egy/legalisation-of-documents"},{"name":"Germany: apostille vs legalisation rule (general)","note":"German Foreign Office states legalisation by the German mission in the issuing state is not needed where an agreement excludes it and an apostille replaces it; in some countries, document checks via administrative assistance replace legalisation. The page does not name Egypt.","country":"Germany","source":"https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/service/-/606802"},{"name":"UAE university description of the attestation chain for certificates issued abroad","note":"University of Birmingham Dubai: certificate certified by issuing authority and local notary, then home-country Ministry of Foreign Affairs, then attested by the UAE embassy in that country, then UAE MoFA. Equivalency for school certificates then goes through UAE Ministry of Education service for certificates issued outside the UAE. Page does not mention Egypt. This is a university page, not the UAE MOE itself.","country":"UAE","source":"https://www.birmingham.ac.uk/dubai/study/apply/entry-requirements/attestation-equivalency"},{"name":"UAE: Thanaweya Amma holders must have certificate attested by UAE MOE","note":"Heriot-Watt Dubai states Thanaweya Al-Amma holders must have their certificates attested by the UAE Ministry of Education; other curricula need MOE equivalency. Students get one semester to obtain equivalency; recognition must happen before joining and university may withdraw enrolment if not obtained in time. Page does not describe the Egyptian-side chain.","country":"UAE","source":"https://www.hw.ac.uk/dubai/study/apply/ministry-of-education-equivalency.htm"},{"name":"Turkey: apostille or approval of foreign diploma for equivalency","note":"Turkish MEB Los Angeles page says education documents must be originals with an authorised signature/approval, and graduates need an original signed diploma with apostille plus transcript. Page says nothing about legalisation, translation or Egypt. Uskudar University page (not official) says diploma must be apostilled or officially approved by relevant authorities and equivalency is applied for via e-Denklik at Turkish embassies abroad. For Egypt, which is not in the Apostille table, the Turkish rule for non-apostille countries is not stated on any page opened.","country":"Turkey","source":"https://losangeles.meb.gov.tr/www/equivalency-certificate-application/icerik/133"},{"name":"Spain: Thanaweya Amma needs legalisation and translation","note":"Spanish Ministry of Education equivalence table lists the Thanaweya a' Amma (General Secondary Education Certificate) as matching Titulo de Bachiller and says it 'Precisa de legalizacion y de traduccion', with a fee.","country":"All","source":"https://educacionfpydeportes.gob.es/dam/jcr:ed20993a-f46e-4f5e-b53e-01e84b48ace0/egipto.pdf"},{"name":"UK embassies cannot translate documents","note":"GOV.UK states British embassies cannot translate documents; find a qualified translator. The page is about UK documents used abroad and does not mention Egypt.","country":"UK","source":"https://www.gov.uk/notarial-and-documentary-services-guide-for-egypt"},{"name":"Germany: uni-assist document instructions for Egyptian applicants","note":"uni-assist Egypt page: private school diploma assessed under ZAB guidelines; Al-Azhar applicants need leaving certificate plus other certificates such as enrolment proof; Nile International Secondary Education applicants need school certificate, Egyptian university enrolment certificate, Tansik Nomination Card showing final average, national exam certificates in religious and national education. Page does not mention translation or legalisation.","country":"Germany","source":"https://www.uni-assist.de/en/tools/info-country-by-country/details-country/country/eg/"}],"foreign_views":[{"body":"University of Basel (Switzerland), country list for 2026/2027","statement":"Lists Egypt: 'Thanaweya a'Amma (General Secondary Education Certificate GSEC)', plus 80% average, current proof of a place in the desired subject at a recognised Egyptian university, and the Swiss supplementary exam (ECUS).","source":"https://www.unibas.ch/dam/jcr:6356e4e7-d6e5-4982-a935-27230134d796/Laenderliste_auslaendische_Vorbildungsausweise_akademisches_Jahr_2026_2027_mit%20Links_pdf.2026-01-19-10-04-18.pdf","country":"Switzerland","system":"thanaweya-amma"},{"body":"University of Winnipeg (Canada), countries A-Z","statement":"Egypt secondary credential: 'General Secondary School Certificate Examination, Thanaweya a'ama'.","source":"https://uwinnipeg.ca/future-student/international/countries-a-to-z/-e-.html","country":"Canada","system":"thanaweya-amma"},{"body":"anabin (Kultusministerkonferenz), Egypt news item, evaluation published 15.03.2022, KMK decision 25.11.2021","country":"Germany","statement":"Lists three Thanaweya Amma certificates (Literary section, Scientific section mathematics, Scientific section science), acquired from 2014. For Literary and Mathematics: access 'ueber Feststellungspruefung/Studienkolleg' to the matching subject course at all universities, if the certificate shows at least 60% of the maximum total points and specified subjects are documented. Science section: same route for all subject courses. Holders who additionally prove at least one year of successful university study get direct subject-specific admission to the previous field and related subjects at all universities (per anabin, applies to all three sections). New rules apply from Wintersemester 2022/2023. No direct admission from the certificate alone. Egyptian Baccalaureate not mentioned. Opened via summarising fetch tool, so exact wording of conditions should be re-read on the page.","system":"thanaweya-amma","source":"https://anabin2.kmk.org/filter/news/newsdetails/artikel//aegypten.html"},{"body":"Goethe-Institut Dubai Studienkolleg FAQ (describes the Studienkolleg Egypt route)","country":"Germany","statement":"Cites the Thanaweya Amma of the mathematical-technical or natural science branch as an example of a secondary certificate that does not give direct university access; holders need Studienkolleg plus a German B1 certificate submitted by June 30; applications via uni-assist; then maths entrance test. Studienkolleg Egypt is held in person at Goethe-Institut Cairo (2022/23 fee 105,000 EGP). Page does not mention legalisation or translation.","system":"thanaweya-amma","source":"https://goethe.de/ins/ae/en/spr/klg/faq.html"},{"body":"uni-assist, Egypt country page","country":"Germany","statement":"One year of accredited university study qualifies for a Studienkolleg; two years qualifies for a bachelor course (page text: subject area of previous study). Page has sections for private high school diploma, Al-Azhar, Nile International certificate, and private university study; it has no section on the Thanaweya Amma or the Egyptian Baccalaureate. Nile International Secondary Education certificate holders with university enrolment are stated to qualify for a Studienkolleg.","system":"both","source":"https://www.uni-assist.de/en/tools/info-country-by-country/details-country/country/eg/"},{"body":"DAAD, Egypt data and analysis 2021 (Daten und Analysen)","country":"Germany","statement":"Describes Thanaweya Amma as the Egyptian general university entrance qualification after three years at Gymnasium, with three streams (science, mathematics, literary/language). States 2021 minimum for best state universities fell by about 10 percent: 88.4% science, 80% mathematics, 65% literary. States 74% passed in 2020/2021 versus 81% the year before. Does not say how it is recognised in Germany.","system":"thanaweya-amma","source":"https://www.daad.de/app/bsa/pdf/long/65/current/"},{"body":"Spanish Ministry of Education equivalence table for Egypt","country":"All","statement":"Thanaweya a' Amma (General Secondary Education Certificate, GSEC) reached in third year of secondary; grade scale numeric 0 to 100 (no decimals); minimum pass 50. Tracks and subjects not stated. Matched to Titulo de Bachiller.","system":"thanaweya-amma","source":"https://educacionfpydeportes.gob.es/dam/jcr:ed20993a-f46e-4f5e-b53e-01e84b48ace0/egipto.pdf"},{"body":"Dalhousie University (Canada), international admissions requirements by country","country":"Canada","statement":"Egypt entry lists Thanaweya a'Amma (General Secondary Education Certificate) as the equivalent qualification; admission also depends on subjects studied and grades. Egyptian Baccalaureate not mentioned. University page, not a federal body.","system":"thanaweya-amma","source":"https://www.dal.ca/admissions/how-to-apply/undergraduate-admissions/international-applicants/international-admissions-requirements-by-country.html"},{"body":"Montclair State University (USA), international high school equivalency table","country":"USA","statement":"Africa table lists Egypt: 'Certificate of General Secondary Education-Thanawiya Amma' as a qualification treated as equivalent to a US high school diploma. University page, not EducationUSA or a evaluation body.","system":"thanaweya-amma","source":"https://www.montclair.edu/admissions-aid/how-apply-montclair-state-university/international-applicants/international-first-year-applicants/international-transcripts-and-high-school-equivalency-requirements"},{"body":"Cardiff University, Egypt entry requirements (UK)","country":"UK","statement":"Graduates of the national high school system might need an International Foundation Year before undergraduate study; entry otherwise needs a recognised foundation programme or good A-level scores, or one or more years at a recognised Egyptian university may be considered. Thanaweya Amma and Egyptian Baccalaureate not named; no grade given. University page, not UK ENIC.","system":"thanaweya-amma","source":"https://www.cardiff.ac.uk/study/international/your-country/africa/egypt/entry-requirements"},{"body":"Middle East Technical University Northern Cyprus Campus, Egypt page","country":"Turkey","statement":"Requires the General Secondary Education Certificate (Thanwiya Amma) with minimum 65% in the stream related to the programme; other certificates accepted with an equivalency document (Mua'dalah) from Egypt's Ministry of Education. Note this is a Northern Cyprus campus, not a Turkish YOK statement.","system":"both","source":"https://international.ncc.metu.edu.tr/en/admission-criteria-for-your-country/egypt"},{"body":"Egyptian Cairo governorate portal, news of 3 August 2026 quoting the Education Ministry","country":"Egypt","statement":"Describes the Egyptian Baccalaureate as Egypt's official national certificate for completing general secondary education (pre-university), allowing study inside and outside Egypt. It counts for admission to all Egyptian universities through the same coordination as Thanaweya Amma, with the same percentage thresholds for the same overall score. Reports a cooperation agreement with the International Baccalaureate Organization to align it with international benchmarks. Does not state formal recognition by foreign bodies.","system":"egyptian-bac","source":"https://cairo.gov.eg/en/news/2026/august/3/education/"},{"body":"Ahram Online, President Sisi reviews preparations for new academic year","country":"Egypt","statement":"Quotes Education Minister Mohamed Abdel Latif: 'the Baccalaureate curricula have now been accredited by the International Baccalaureate Organization (IBO)'. Page does not mention cohorts.","system":"egyptian-bac","source":"https://english.ahram.org.eg/News/575184.aspx"},{"body":"Ahram Online, New baccalaureate put to the test","country":"Egypt","statement":"Students who pass Grade 9 national exams, or equivalents such as IGCSE, American Diploma, IB or NIS, with 50% overall can enter Grade 10 baccalaureate. It began in Grade 10 in public schools last year; specialisation into four pathways (medicine and life sciences, engineering and computer science, business, arts and humanities) starts this academic year. Ministry spokesman said it is a different system from the IB. No statement on foreign recognition.","system":"egyptian-bac","source":"https://english.ahram.org.eg/News/575757.aspx"},{"body":"AACRAO EDGE news, Egypt introduces baccalaureate (Jan 2025 announcement)","country":"Egypt","statement":"Minister announced the system at a cabinet meeting on 8 January (2025 per article date); it replaces the traditional system for students starting secondary school the next year; three years (core, track choice, advanced). Says it 'includes international recognition' but 'was not specified where the recognition will originate from'.","system":"egyptian-bac","source":"https://www.aacrao.org/edge/emergent-news/egypt-introduces-baccalaureate-certificate-system-as-alternative-to-thanaweya-amma"}],"unverified":["Egypt's status in the Hague Apostille Convention is confirmed only via the HCCH status table (Egypt absent) and Canada's embassy page; I could not open an Egyptian MFA page or the German embassy Cairo page.","The full Egyptian-side chain for a school certificate (Ministry of Education attestation, then Ministry of Foreign Affairs, then destination embassy in Cairo): only the Foreign Ministry then embassy steps are stated by Netherlands, Belgium and Finland pages. No opened official page states a Ministry of Education attestation step. A private site (studienkolleg.org, not official) claims the MoE-MFA-embassy chain; excluded.","German embassy Cairo legalisation page (kairo.diplo.de) failed to load; Germany's rule on whether Egyptian school certificates need legalisation or embassy verification for uni-assist is not confirmed.","Who may translate and into which language for Germany (uni-assist translation page could not be opened); Germany translation rule unverified.","UK ENIC / Ecctis statement about Thanaweya Amma or the Egyptian Baccalaureate: Ecctis methodology page does not mention Egypt; UK ENIC pages not opened. UK embassy Cairo legalisation page not found. UK legalisation and translation rules for Egyptian documents unverified.","USA: no EducationUSA Egypt, WES or NACES page stating the Thanaweya Amma view was reached; only a university equivalence table and a translation-agency blog (excluded). US embassy Cairo authentication guidance not found.","Canada: no federal or provincial credential-evaluation page (CICIC, WES Canada) on Egyptian certificates opened; Canada's legalisation requirement for Egyptian documents unverified.","Turkey: no YOK page and no Turkish embassy Cairo page readable (embassy file was binary). Equivalency rule for Egyptian diplomas and how Turkey treats a non-apostille country unverified.","UAE: UAE MOE site pages were not opened; UAE views come from university pages (Heriot-Watt Dubai, Birmingham Dubai).","Germany and the Egyptian Baccalaureate: anabin and uni-assist pages opened do not mention it, so its German treatment is unverified. Baccalaureate cohort details (which graduating years) and foreign recognition beyond the IBO accreditation quote are not confirmed on any ministry page; the moe.gov.eg root pages were not opened except via search-result pages.","anabin and AACRAO items were read through a summarising fetch tool; exact wording and the date of the AACRAO Jan 2025 article should be re-checked before quoting.","Thanaweya Amma official structure (which grades count), tracks/branches, exam timing and total-score scale from an Egyptian official source.","Which cohorts the Egyptian Baccalaureate applies to and its first-year start date: not stated on fetched Ministry pages (one page calls it a proposal; others discuss 2026/2027 rules).","Official recognition abroad of the Egyptian Baccalaureate: Ministry says it is internationally recognised and plans to seek accreditation from international bodies; no foreign body statement found.","UK ENIC, EducationUSA/WES, DAAD/anabin pages were not opened (uni-hamburg page blocked by robots; others not reached before rate limit).","AACRAO is a professional association, not a government body; its 2025 report (8 Jan 2025 cabinet announcement, EGP 500 later attempts) conflicts with later Ministry fee of EGP 200 and should not be relied on for fees.","Cairo governorate pages relay Ministry statements via news outlets (Akhbar El Yom, Al-Ahram Gate); the URL for the September page is as returned by search ('septemper') in the original link: https://cairo.gov.eg/en/news/2026/septemper/8/a9e62061cb52415fb12c072e04388db3"]};
